From e2f4140158160ed9f6b434ff3dd14ee042083a25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:16:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] ##asm: USSE pseudo syntax + disassembler tests

Pseudo-C rendering for the usse arch (asm.pseudo=true): mov/ALU ->
"a = b op c", fmad -> "a = b * c + d", ba/br -> "goto", ba.savelink ->
"call", predicate prefixes -> "if (pN) ..."; flagged/memory forms pass
through unchanged.

Add test/db/asm/usse: 21 disassembly regression tests on instructions
written for them, not taken from firmware (all pass via
rasm2 -a usse -b 32).
---
